<div class="archive-intro"><h1>About</h1></div>
<div class="about-content prose">
<p><strong>Haitao Pan, PhD</strong> is a biostatistician and clinical-trial methodologist working at the intersection of oncology, evidence generation, and decision-making.</p>
<p>This is a personal blog for clear, independent writing about the questions that arise between research evidence and clinical decisions.</p>
<p>For information about my research group and institutional work, visit my <a href="https://www.stjude.org/research/labs/pan-lab.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">St. Jude research group page</a>.</p>
<p>You can also <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/haitao-pan-05578a189" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">follow me on LinkedIn</a> for professional updates and new writing.</p>
<p>Views expressed here are personal and do not necessarily represent those of my employer or collaborators.</p>
</div></BaseLayout>
